    "module": "Module 4: Working conditions, governance and leadership",
    "abbreviatedName": "Health workforce governance and leadership capacity",
    "name": "Existence of health workforce governance and leadership capacity at national and/or subnational levels",
    "definition": "This indicator is a composite of five sub-indicators, see below. The response to these five\nsub-indicators is aggregated as a score (see part II on methods) on a scale from 1 (nascent)\nto 5 (sustainable).\nEach sub-indicator is a self-assessment of one aspect of countries’ governance and leadership\ncapacity vis-à-vis of health and care workers. To help answer these self-assessed sub-indicators,\na series of guiding questions are provided.",
    "glossary": "Occupation; Health workforce planning; Lifelong learning; Continuing professional development; In-service training",
    "reportingFrequency": "Every three years",
    "reportingFrameworks": "Global Strategy for Human Resources for Health: Workforce 2030 (GSHRH), Working for Health programme, Global Strategic Directions for Nursing and Midwifery (SDNM)",
    "dataSources": "Ministry of Health, Education, Labour; Regional and/or subnational ministries of health and education; Institutions or units responsible for policies on health workforce; Relevant ministries according to the national government structure and constitutional arrangements/ level of devolution; Educational institutions; Health facilities",
    "furtherInformation": "(6, 9, 52, 53, 63, 86-94)",
